# cuts/v1.0.57/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY v1.0.56, AND WHY THE THREE DEAD VERSIONS BEFORE IT ARE NOT A RACE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three tags died before this one, each at a gate the previous never reached:
#
#   v1.0.53   REFUSED AT PREFLIGHT     four tree conditions at its own commit
#   v1.0.54   preflight PASSED         died in-build at check-orphans
#   v1.0.55   preflight passed TWICE   died in-build at check-freshness
#
# THE GATES RUN IN SERIES INSIDE THE BUILD, after signing credentials import.
# There is no pre-tag sweep that answers "will this cut survive", so each
# version buys exactly one gate's worth of information. Four versions have now
# walked four gates. That is the honest reading, and it is not a race anyone
# lost: the invariant is
#
#     A CUT TAG MUST BE CREATED AFTER EVERY CONDITION IT WILL BE JUDGED ON.
#
# 🔴 LIVE-READ VERSUS TREE-READ IS WHAT DECIDES WHETHER A VERSION IS SPENT.
# check-orphans and check-pr-age read LIVE GitHub state at build time, so
# CLOSING a PR clears them with no new version -- that is how v1.0.55 attempt 2
# was bought for free. check-freshness's remedy (a hold_ack or a re-pin) lives
# in the TREE, so main necessarily moves past the tag and the tag becomes
# permanently unsatisfiable. That forced this version. Anyone tempted to
# "just re-run" v1.0.55 should read that sentence twice.
#
# ⚠️ AND PART OF IT WAS SELF-INFLICTED: two of v1.0.55's three stale pins were
# advanced by our OWN merges earlier the same night (CM041 #135, CM044 #266).
# Merging upstream INSIDE a cut window advances the live HEADs the pins are
# measured against, so the cut's inputs went stale underneath it. Merging
# upstream during a cut is not free.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DAEMON_COMMIT -- DELIBERATELY NOT ADVANCED. Do not "tidy" this line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# c6fc48c0 is hub-v0.4.69, the same daemon v1.0.54 and v1.0.55 named. THIS CUT
# REBUILDS NO DAEMON, so advancing it would claim a build that does not exist.
# Both halves of that release remain published (ostler-releases serves the
# daemon, ostler-assistant serves the hub app, BOTH fetched at the same
# DAEMON_RELEASE_TAG) and nothing about them has changed since v1.0.54.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT CARRIES -- FOUR of Andy's six, up from ONE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   A2 (#454)  Settings "Advanced" section removed        oa #369, carried since v1.0.54
#   A3 (#218)  settling panel li-row renderer             CM044 #266, via image re-pin
#   A5 (#594)  "Duplicate review ... Hub Mac only"        CM044 #262, via image re-pin
#   #659       a real name beats a social handle          CM041 #134, grafted verbatim
#
# THE WIKI PAIR IS THE REASON THIS CUT IS WORTH ITS VERSION. Both were merged
# upstream BEFORE v1.0.54 and reached NEITHER previous cut, because the wiki
# renderer ships as a pinned image and merged is not delivered. CM044 v0.1.29
# was built and published for this cut and install.sh now pins its two digests.
# Clearing that RED by hold_ack instead would have shipped v1.0 with dup-review
# and corrections still dead on the Hub, purely to avoid moving a digest.
#
# 🟢 BOTH DIGESTS VERIFIED BY AUTHENTICATED MANIFEST READ, two-sided:
#   tag 0.1.29 -> exactly the two digests install.sh now pins        MATCH
#   tag 0.1.28 -> exactly the two digests being REPLACED             MATCH
#   a 64-zero digest                                                 404
# The 0.1.28 control is the strong one: the tag being replaced resolves to the
# digest being replaced, so the re-pin demonstrably moves from the right old
# value to the right new one. ⚠️ THE TAGS CARRY NO "v" PREFIX -- the registry
# holds 0.1.24 through 0.1.29. Asking for v0.1.29 returns 404 and reads
# identically to a failed push. That cost one CANNOT-RUN before it was found.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT DOES NOT CARRY -- stated so the walk is not a surprise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   A4 (#482)  Bursar usage-journal roster. ANDY'S SCOPE CALL. Two of the five
#              required producers do not exist, and both live in repos that
#              call models, so the meter is missing exactly where spend
#              happens. Demoting the roster to obtain a green has been proposed
#              twice and refused twice: it converts a true "we are not
#              measuring this" into a false "everything is measured".
#   A6 (#300)  dedupe. NOW ARCHAEOLOGY, not deferred. CM041 #135 is the
#              discriminator v1052-D006 recorded as NOT RUN; it was run against
#              the SHIPPING resolver (executed module path asserted, not
#              inferred) and two records sharing one email with different given
#              names land in review, never auto, with the identical-name
#              positive control still auto-merging. So the ~30 over-merges are
#              historical damage, no future install reproduces it, and the
#              repair of rows already written is an OPERATOR decision.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE, AND THAT IS CORRECT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.56.tsv does not exist, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly not conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release is a
# prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to its current target.
# The sequence is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote.
#
# ⚠️ PUT THE DMG IN THE WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks in
# only $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop and $HOME of the ssh user it walks as,
# and on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES artefact_sha256_source to read
# measured(...). A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere produces PROMOTE=0 for a
# reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than "wrong folder".

CUT_VERSION=1.0.57
DAEMON_COMMIT=c6fc48c0
CM051=ce25d6f56743c5e66d82fbb5c3b8e44a5eac375a
